/* 6. [28p] THE FIRST-WRONG FLASH — red, glowing, and STILL TAPPABLE.
   Yasir: "1st wrong must flash a RED GLOW on a still-live card; disabling/greying belongs ONLY at 2
   wrong attempts. Today it is the opposite." My 28e ruling ("a disabled option is never red") was right
   but landed on `.crossed`, the class used for BOTH the momentary buzz and the permanent lock, so it
   bleached the first-wrong feedback too. `.wrong-flash` restores red where it belongs; 28e's grey lock
   on `.crossed` from the 2nd attempt is untouched.
   pointer-events stays AUTO on purpose: on a first miss nothing is taken away, the child may retry the
   same card. It is removed after 700ms by app.js. */
