/* ---- आगे: the reference's NAV-NEXT-BTN + NAV-PULSE, verbatim, then this engine's boxes: 170x62 on the tutorial pages, 190x62
   elsewhere (the reference's), in the places this file already gives the button; a page that hides the button inline keeps it
   hidden (the reference's pick pages do that with a card flag) ---- */
/* [NAV-NEXT-BTN] (2026-09-24) pages 2-14: the आगे pill (#navBtn) is drawn by the user's next-button art instead of its text, in the
   SAME box at the SAME spot on every page (the button's own box is untouched: 170x62 at bottom 128 on the story pages, 190x62 at
   bottom 20 on the question pages, 190x62 at bottom 80 on the train pages - so the आगे hand nudge, placed from that box, is
   untouched too). Two states, one box:
   - not .active: the DISABLED art (btn-next-disabled: grey #EDEDED pill, grey arrow) is VISIBLE wherever the text pill was not - it
     replaces the old opacity:0 / visibility:hidden of the inactive pill AND the display:none the pick pages (mountTapOptions) and
     the train pages (before their last match) set inline - with no functionality: pointer-events:none and the disabled attribute
     as before;
   - .active (setNavActive(true): the moment आगे used to fade in): the ENABLED art (btn-next: yellow #FCB717 pill, navy arrow) fades in
     over the disabled one in the same .3 s, and the tap does exactly what it did (the slide's onclick).
   The art is two layers on two pseudo-elements (::before = disabled, ::after = enabled; the old "→" content of ::after is gone):
   the PILL (btn-next(-disabled)-pill.svg, preserveAspectRatio none) drawn at 100% x 100% of a canvas = the button's border box +
   the art's 14 px shadow margin all round (insets -17 px: 14 + the 3 px border, since insets count from the padding box), so the
   pill fills the box exactly whether it is 170 or 190 wide, and the ARROW (btn-next(-disabled)-arrow.svg) at its own 40x28 size
   centred, never stretched. The user's originals (btn-next.svg / btn-next-disabled.svg) are kept beside them unused. The pill's own
   fill, border colour, box-shadows and text are switched off (the art has its own shadow; the text is the accessible name only).
   The end screen keeps the button away exactly as before (body.is-end #navBtn{display:none}), and so does the title screen
   (body.is-start: its start gate is transparent, so the stage would show through); the train pages 13-14 show no disabled art
   either - see the last two rules. */
#navBtn:not([style*="display: none"]){display:flex !important;background:transparent !important;border-color:transparent !important;box-shadow:none !important;
  color:transparent !important;font-size:0 !important;opacity:1 !important;visibility:visible !important;overflow:visible !important;}
#navBtn:not(.active){box-shadow:none !important;pointer-events:none !important;cursor:default !important;}
#navBtn::before,#navBtn::after{content:"" !important;position:absolute;left:-17px;right:-17px;top:-17px;bottom:-17px;pointer-events:none;font-size:0;
  background-repeat:no-repeat,no-repeat;background-position:center,center;background-size:40px 28px,100% 100%;transition:opacity .3s ease;}
#navBtn::before{background-image:url("assets/UI/btn-next-disabled-arrow.svg"),url("assets/UI/btn-next-disabled-pill.svg");opacity:1;}
#navBtn::after{background-image:url("assets/UI/btn-next-arrow.svg"),url("assets/UI/btn-next-pill.svg");opacity:0;}
#navBtn.active::after{opacity:1;}
#navBtn.active::before{opacity:0;}
body.is-end #navBtn{display:none !important;}
/* Page 1 (2026-09-24, bak107): the title screen's start gate is TRANSPARENT there (body.is-start .start-gate{background:transparent};
   the body carries the sky), so the stage behind it shows through - the disabled art, visible since display:flex above, appeared
   under the landing card. The landing has no आगे at all, so the button stays out of the page while body.is-start (dropped once the
   tutorial has mounted, so page 2 gets it back); pages 2-14 are unchanged. */
body.is-start #navBtn{display:none !important;}
/* Pages 13-14 (2026-09-24, bak109, [TRAIN-NAV-AFTER-DEPART]): the train pages (slide.ref_frame -> .stage.ref-frame) show NO disabled
   art. The BLANK_PANEL module hides the button inline (style.display none) from mount until the train has left the panel and only
   then shows + activates it (showNav at the end of the refTrainOut run, fallback 6.3 s) - the display:flex above had overridden
   that inline none. So here the button stays out of the page while it is not .active, and the enabled art appears in the same
   190x62 box at bottom 80 the moment the module activates it, exactly where the disabled art stood. Pages 2-12 are unchanged. */
.stage.ref-frame #navBtn:not(.active){display:none !important;}
/* [P5-NO-NAV] (2026-10-01) page 5 (G1 = ?slide=3; card slide.hide_nav -> .stage.no-nav, set in mountSlide like hide_header_chip): the
   disabled आगे art at the bottom of the page is removed on this page - the pick page advances by itself on the correct tap and
   never activates the button, so nothing is lost; the button's box, wiring and every other page are untouched. Later that day, on
   request, the other seven pick pages (pages 6-12 = G2, G3, G4, P1, P2, P3, P4 = ?slide=4..10) carry the same card flag, so no pick
   page shows the disabled art any more; the story pages 2-4 and the train pages 13-14 are as they were. */
.stage.no-nav #navBtn{display:none !important;}
/* [NAV-PULSE] (2026-10-09, user request; re-timed the same day): the moment आगे is ENABLED it pulsates like the title page's
   play button does once it is ready ([LANDING-START-AFTER-VO] .sg-breathe -> sgBtnPulse, line ~544: scale 1 -> 1.04 -> 1,
   1.4 s ease-in-out, repeating) - the same keyframes, timing and amplitude, on every page where the button exists (story pages
   2-4 once आगे appears, train pages 13-14 once the train has left; the pick pages never enable it). "Enabled" is #navBtn.active,
   which setNavActive(true) sets at the same instant it clears `disabled` (the kit's reveal hold and the pages' first-tap rule
   still decide WHEN that happens - untouched). The pulse runs on the ENABLED art layer (#navBtn::after = btn-next-pill + arrow,
   which already covers the pill and its shadow margin), not on the button box: the box keeps its translateX(-50%) centring and
   its hover lift / press transforms exactly as before (sgBtnPulse itself carries translateX(-50%) for the same reason; a `scale`
   on the box would scale that translate and the pill would drift sideways on every beat), the disabled art (::before) never
   moves, and the hit area is unchanged. The 4.5 s hand nudge (nudgeNavBtn) is left as it is; on pages 2-4 [P2-QUIET-AFTER-NAV]
   still suppresses that hand - this breathe is the one repeating motion the user asked for there. Still mode (html.no-anim,
   prefers-reduced-motion) stops it, as the landing holds its disc still. (The first version of this block used the sentence
   chip's cue pulse, 1.10 at .8 s; superseded by this one at the user's ask.) */
@keyframes navBreathe{0%,100%{scale:1;}50%{scale:1.04;}}
#navBtn.active::after{animation:navBreathe 1.4s ease-in-out infinite;transform-origin:50% 50%;will-change:scale;}
#navBtn:not(.active)::after{animation:none;scale:1;}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ #navBtn.active::after{animation:none;scale:1;} }
html.no-anim #navBtn.active::after{animation:none !important;scale:1;}

